{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters","id":1338257,"title":"How come no one told me Socialites get to make extra characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-28T06:17:02-07:00","id":1338257,"title":"How come no one told me Socialites get to make extra characters?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Well Well, not literally. Because we don't talk like we used to. We've grown apart. <i>To say I had no regrets would be a lie...</i></span><br /> <br /> But seriously, I've just been reading through Socialize fully instead of skimming- I used to play a Socialize and Bureaucracy main in Ex2.5 so i skipped over it this time, and as ST, none of my players went into. So imagine my surprise when I get to <b>Heart-Eclipsing Shroud</b>, which lets you swap out all your intimacies to stroll about as a new person/ False Persona. No big deal, right? Kinda cool. <br /> <br /> Well then <b>Hundred-Faced Stranger</b> gives each persona its own Abilities and Specialties (which also earns you xp back!). And then <b>Legend Mask Methodology </b>lets you buy charms for the persona <i>that the real you might not even qualify for</i>. It should be noted that each persona <b><i>has half your total xp to invest</i></b>. And then it gets <b>bumped up to 75%</b>, with an xp earned booster as well!<br /> <br /> From there, forget about painstaking persona crafting, you can just make a new <b><i>right out of thin air</i></b> with <i>At Your Service</i>. Does that damned fool in your way Peleps Jadko need you to be a Pirate Captain? well now you are, with Sail, Larceny, and whatever the hell else you need. Cynis Juliet is Heartbroken? You are now a world renowned musician Sesus Romeo with a specialty in love songs. <i>you can do this in front of people </i>and they will just <b><i>retcon the change away</i></b>. The Penultimate Charm, <b>Fugue-Empowering Other</b> lets you pull use any charm or ability you have from another one of your personas (who are, btw, at 3/4ths the xp of your &quot;real&quot; character) whenever you need it... and finally, the capstone. Soul Reprisal. <br /> <br /> Before I talk about <b>Soul Reprisal</b>, I want to mention the Craft Charm <b>Dual Magus Prana</b>. DMP lets you declare, upon death, that Surprise! you are fine and the enemy actually killed a puppet/hologram/doombot version of you. For a long time, people on this forum debated whether this was cheap or OP or not. I bring that up because <b><i>Soul Reprisal</i></b> let's you pull a weird inversion of that trick. When you are killed, you- and I swear this is exactly how its described- <i>grab your own Exaltation and forcibly incarnate it into your own body again as if your false persona was the next host</i>. Fuck me, that is the coolest thing ever. You get back a few health boxes and keep playing as one of your False Personas who is at 3/4ths total xp, still part of the story, has up to 4 other False Personas ready to go. If you hate your ST, you could even make your original personality <i>another False Persona</i>. <br /> <br /> I want to try it so bad. If you Supernal Socia<span style=\"font-size:14px\">lize you essentially get your main character and 1~5 other characters at a comparable powe</span>r level to you. In fact, you can even just keep the personas at baseline without too much investment because <i><u>each persona grants you 2 xp for every 3 you earn</u>. </i>Its worded kind of obtusely, but it seems like having a persona makes you level up faster, and since you can have up to five, that means and 8 xp session earns you [ 8+ (2*5) ] 18 xp per session. Each one comes with a measly xp investment too of rebuying one charm(<span style=\"font-size:8px\">you do terrible damage to your characters psyche though<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">). Y</span></span></span>ou can keep the xp or invest it into your personas. <br /> <br /> <b>Yet I've never seen any discussion about any of this on the forum</b>. What do you think about this? I think it's really flavorful and cool. It also comes built in with a bunch of story hooks about how much Limit your poor mind gains and how Intimacies get tangled up in you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T06:24:06-07:00","id":1338258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet I've <b>never</b> seen<b> any </b>discussion about <b>any of this</b> on the forum. What do you think about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just made a thread about my experience with such a character. It\u2019s still on the front page and everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T06:29:57-07:00","id":1338260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e\"> In Which Alucard Discusses Personas... (Exalted 3e) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335355-in-which-alucard-discusses-personas-exalted-3e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Because someone in Ask a Question, Get an Answer (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1335231#post1335231) </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Here is a link to it. Good read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T06:44:05-07:00","id":1338262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to try it so bad. If you Supernal Socia<span style=\"font-size:14px\">lize you essentially get your main character and 1~5 other characters at a comparable powe</span>r level to you. In fact, you can even just keep the personas at baseline without too much investment because <i><u>each persona grants you 2 xp for every 3 you earn</u>. </i>Its worded kind of obtusely, but it seems like having a persona makes you level up faster, and since you can have up to five, that means and 8 xp session earns you [ 8+ (2*5) ] 18 xp per session. Each one comes with a measly xp investment too of rebuying one charm(<span style=\"font-size:8px\">you do terrible damage to your characters psyche though<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">). Y</span></span></span>ou can keep the xp or invest it into your personas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The experience points a Persona gains are its own, your true self doesn't earn them. Each persona has its own Experience track. When your Persona gains 2 experience for every 3 you gain, it means the persona earns 2 for its own Charms / Attributes / Abilities every time you earn 3 (Whenever you earn experience it's always the &quot;true&quot; you who earns experience, Personas only ever gain experience through the effects of the Persona Charms)<br /> <br /> Also don't underestimate the drawbacks, such as having multiple Limit Triggers, having Persona Intimacies bleed into your main personality, the Persona's stats being limited by your points in Integrity or Presence, Bureaucracy or Linguistics, Ride or Sail, Socialize, and one Dawn Caste Ability, and the Persona being unable to surpass you in Craft, Occult, Lore and combat as a whole. Basically there is a very specific optimal character spread you need to make to truly leverage personas.<br /> <br /> Not trying to discourage you from making a Personas character, they look like a lot of fun, just trying to keep your expectations at a realistic level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T07:52:38-07:00","id":1338272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then <b>Hundred-Faced Stranger</b> gives each persona its own Abilities and Specialties (which also earns you xp back!).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also very sharply-limited, and can even potentially lock you out of your native Charms. If you're Brawl 5 in your base self, and you allot only one point of Brawl to one of your Personas, then you won't be able to use those awesome punch techniques you invested so much XP into.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Incidentally, depending on your ST, you're going to want to lock five of those Ability dots into Socialize <i>immediately</i>, because otherwise you might not be able to switch back.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then <b>Legend Mask Methodology </b>lets you buy charms for the persona <i>that the real you might not even qualify for</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, one thing to be wary of is the possibility that you approach a scenario wearing one persona, and find that it probably would've been better to have done it as somebody else; that four hour switch-time can be inconvenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From there, forget about painstaking persona crafting, you can just make a new <b><i>right out of thin air</i></b> with <i>At Your Service</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not accurate; you're not creating it out of thin air; you're piecing it together out of the personas you've <i>already</i> created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Penultimate Charm, <b>Fugue-Empowering Other</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to personally thank you for using &quot;penultimate&quot; correctly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a long time, people on this forum debated whether this was cheap or OP or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally my perception has been that these &quot;debates&quot; often existed to serve the larger purpose of shitting on the craft system in specific or on Ex3 in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck me, that is the coolest thing ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about solving a murder while discovering the identity of the Emissary of Nexus at the same time? Or accidentally knocking out your teammate with Mists of Eventide and puppeteering him to keep fighting the Fair Folk you were trying to gas? Or forcing some of your own brain cells to die through sheer force of will to block out a horrifying revelation about how one of your teammates perceives reality?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you hate your ST, you could even make your original personality <i>another False Persona</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you hate your ST, you probably shouldn't be playing with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to try it so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give it a shot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:06:58-07:00","id":1338275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338258#post1338258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just made a thread about my experience with such a character. It\u2019s still on the front page and everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is my bad. I only check in once or twice a week and binge read. At time of posting your thread was down at the bottom among stuff i already read and i missed it. Whoops. Thanks for thanking me about penultimate. Its one of my favorite words to use properly, along with ostensibly. And peruse. And plethora. And pristine. And\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:17:09-07:00","id":1338277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338262#post1338262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The experience points a Persona gains are its own, your true self doesn't earn them. Each persona has its own Experience track. When your Persona gains 2 experience for every 3 you gain, it means the persona earns 2 for its own Charms / Attributes / Abilities every time you earn 3 (Whenever you earn experience it's always the &amp;quot;true&amp;quot; you who earns experience, Personas only ever gain experience through the effects of the Persona Charms)<br /> <br /> Also don't underestimate the drawbacks, such as having multiple Limit Triggers, having Persona Intimacies bleed into your main personality, the Persona's stats being limited by your points in Integrity or Presence, Bureaucracy or Linguistics, Ride or Sail, Socialize, and one Dawn Caste Ability, and the Persona being unable to surpass you in Craft, Occult, Lore and combat as a whole. Basically there is a very specific optimal character spread you need to make to truly leverage personas.<br /> <br /> Not trying to discourage you from making a Personas character, they look like a lot of fun, just trying to keep your expectations at a realistic level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i misread that in my haste. Thev wording in Hundred Faced Stranger makes more sense now. <br /> <br /> The abilities arent too much hindrance, i guess, because afterwards you get half your xp to spend on them. But the restraints are there to keep you from making a pocket Dawn. Still its cool to have Sail, Performance, or Linguistics as charmsets when you need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:59:13-07:00","id":1338284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338272#post1338272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally my perception has been that these &quot;debates&quot; often existed to serve the larger purpose of shitting on the craft system in specific or on Ex3 in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty as charged. (I don't, thematically, like Doombot-style Charms.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338277#post1338277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The abilities arent too much hindrance, i guess, because afterwards you get half your xp to spend on them. But the restraints are there to keep you from making a pocket Dawn. Still its cool to have Sail, Performance, or Linguistics as charmsets <b>when you need them</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>When do you need them?<br /> <br /> As a Socailize Supernal, do you not already have these Abilities?<br /> If you don't, do you not have a Circle-mate who has them?<br /> If you don't, do you have four hours to put your Persona on to get them?<br /> <br /> Hundred Faced Stranger is a good Charm because it makes your Personas more convincing. I don't rate it as a utility belt.<br /> <br /> But it's not like my opinion is based on extensive play experience. I bow to The Count on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-28-2019, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T10:46:11-07:00","id":1338319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338272#post1338272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(Incidentally, depending on your ST, you're going to want to lock five of those Ability dots into Socialize <i>immediately</i>, because otherwise you might not be able to switch back.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to point out that, although the devs seem to have gone back and forth on this question, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1338314#post1338314\">most recent word on this</a> is that you <i>don't</i> need Socialize 5 to revert to your base persona.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T14:10:48-07:00","id":1338333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338319#post1338319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to point out that, although the devs seem to have gone back and forth on this question, the most recent word on this is that you <b>don't</b> need Socialize 5 to revert to your base persona.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you; this is genuinely good news, as while <i>I</i> like Grant Morrison, I imagine not everyone wants to play out the &quot;Batman of Zur-En-Arrh&quot; arc of <i>Batman R.I.P.</i>, let alone be <i>forced </i>to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T15:17:27-07:00","id":1338338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1338333#post1338333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you; this is genuinely good news [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured it was relevant to your interests, yeah, in addition to this thread. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T22:06:52-07:00","id":1338397,"title":"","content":"To the OP on what the goal of Personas were, I generally assumed they come from stories like <i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>, <i>The Great Gatsby</i>, <i>Catch Me if You Can</i>, and even a bit of <i>Le Miserables</i>. Basically putting up such elaborate, all-encompassing fronts you start to trick yourself.<br /> <br /> I think their mechanical implementations are kind of a mess (I did my own housrules on them for a reason) but the ideas pretty sweet IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T08:47:39-07:00","id":1338464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For a long time, people on this forum debated whether this was cheap or OP or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not keen on the execution, but I prefer it to Immortal Malevolence Enslavement and Final Ray of Light from last edition because most PC deaths I've seen were the result of the Storyteller either getting sloppy or overly agressive with encounter design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T11:47:55-07:00","id":1339034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters#post1338257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Yet I've never seen any discussion about any of this on the forum</b>. What do you think about this? I think it's really flavorful and cool. It also comes built in with a bunch of story hooks about how much Limit your poor mind gains and how Intimacies get tangled up in you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was discussed a lot when the books first came out, though mostly from a theorcrafting angle. In terms of why discussion as mostly theorycrafting...<br /> <br /> It is very, very deep into its tree. To learn Legend Mask Methodology, you're nine charms in, plus E3, Socialize 5, and you really want at least one more charm for Draw the Curtain, too. The personas can of course recoup some of that investment, but only some - they have a lot of restrictions - so it really only makes sense if you're already going to go deep into Socialize and intend to use its prerequisites. These things limit the games where it actually comes up in play - it's not something someone can just dip into because they think it's a neat trick, basically. And that's not even getting into the prerequisites for <i>At Your Service</i>, the best charm in that subtree, which requires nearly all of Socialize.<br /> <br /> Also compare to summoning, which can be obtained with literally just one purchase and gives you access to a massive toolkit - sure, not quite as strong as a dedicated Solar, but your demons or elementals can do things independently, which is often more valuable, plus at E3 (when Legend Mask Methodology first comes online) you're able to summon Second Circle Demons. Granted those have restrictions and limitations and drawbacks of their own, but when you compare the relative investment it's pretty clear which one a player is going to go with if they just want a big toolkit of options quickly.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's flavorful and cool, but it's also gated in a way that means that it only comes up occasionally and which makes it so it's only really tempting for players who <i>really</i> want that story. Whereas, say, demons come up constantly because they're both powerful and easy to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-02-2019, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T12:34:14-07:00","id":1339037,"title":"","content":"Doombot charm is only iffy to me because you can't actually make a Doombot, unless it was N/A FAA. Other than that, the shorthand kind of charm doesn't irk me much.<br /> <br /> The Revan charm is cool and good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T11:26:41-07:00","id":1345281,"title":"","content":"Also, the final charm is obviously Dr Who reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:10:00-07:00","id":1345292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338257-how-come-no-one-told-me-socialites-get-to-make-extra-characters?p=1345281#post1345281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the final charm is obviously Dr Who reincarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, I wouldn't really say it's <i>that</i> close to Dr. Who-style regeneration. Dr. Who always comes back as a basically new person who hasn't previously existed (though with some continuity with previous incarnations), whereas the return from death from Soul Reprisal requires you to use a pre-existing persona, a &quot;person&quot; who's already been around, done things, and is known to people. I suppose you could, technically, use one of your persona slots to create a persona that was custom-built to be a good reincarnation, and never actually use it previous to activating Soul Reprisal. I'd probably call shenanigans if you made that too close to your &quot;real&quot; personality, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}